      "appliedContentFormat": "html",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "3396998",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:5f6efc8d-c500-4911-8b8a-d4435f7d3fa6",
            "displayName": "Nithish Gowda"
          },
          "body": "<p data-local-id=\"a2c2f4e41cf0\">Hello,</p><p data-local-id=\"3ab70bc4c972\">Thank you for contacting Appriss Retail Support.</p><p data-local-id=\"e11c7086c055\">We’ve received your ticket and are routing it to the appropriate team for assistance. The assigned representative will follow up as soon as they’ve had a chance to review.</p><p data-local-id=\"a23762b90af0\">Kind Regards,</p><p data-local-id=\"1d924778016d\">Appriss Retail Support </p>",
          "created": "2026-10-15T13:58:49.905-0400",
          "updated": "2026-10-15T13:58:49.905-0400",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "accountId": "712020:5f6efc8d-c500-4911-8b8a-d4435f7d3fa6",
            "displayName": "Nithish Gowda"
          },
          "jsdPublic": true
        },
        {
          "id": "3397002",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "5f8852df6932330076610600",
            "displayName": "Nick Hawkins"
          },
          "body": "<p>🤖 Talos triage · confidence: medium</p><p><strong>Talos can make mistakes. Please check important information.</strong></p><p><strong>Verdict</strong><br>No known or recurring incident matches, and nothing I read points to a code defect. The six users share a pattern (office, hub and distribution center staff), so the check is whether the sign-in data for them carries a level and a store assignment.</p><p><strong>What we checked</strong></p><ul><li><p>Nothing in the client&#039;s notes or the cross-client known-incident list matches this symptom.</p></li><li><p>At each sign-in the security level is taken from the first of these that has a value: a level set in Secure&#039;s SSO admin screen, the level sent by the customer&#039;s sign-in system, or a configured default. If none has a value, the level stays blank.</p></li><li><p>No default level is set up for this client. The setting that would supply one is not present for Tailored Brands.</p></li><li><p>A user&#039;s store assignments are rebuilt at each sign-in from the store list the customer&#039;s sign-in system sends. If a user&#039;s sign-in carries no store, their store hierarchy stays empty. That fits the users who have no single store (office, hub, distribution center).</p></li><li><p>This client&#039;s setup maps users to Incident security levels by team membership. Users who are not in one of the listed teams would get no level from that mapping.</p></li><li><p>The &quot;daily SSO file&quot; is not something I could find in the code. I could not confirm which feed sets the level, and I could not see what was sent for these six users.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Next</strong></p><ul><li><p>Compare what the customer&#039;s sign-in system sent for one affected user (for example Chris Orth) with a user whose level and stores show correctly.</p></li><li><p>Check whether the six users are in a team listed in the client&#039;s Incident mapping, and whether their sign-in carries any store or hierarchy values.</p></li></ul>",
          "created": "2026-10-15T14:03:37.002-0400",
          "updated": "2026-10-15T14:03:37.002-0400",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "accountId": "5f8852df6932330076610600",
            "displayName": "Nick Hawkins"
          },
          "jsdPublic": false
        },
        {
          "id": "3397050",
          "author": {
            "accountId": "712020:688bd119-6d13-450b-95ac-b1ef3fbb547b",
            "displayName": "Juan Martinez"
          },
          "body": "<p data-local-id=\"0f09835899fd\"><strong>Escalating to Secure Engineering.</strong> The Incident security level from SSO+ is not applied on the sign in that creates the user. Matthew Kamminga confirmed on Teams on 2026-10-15 that it should apply on creation and on later sign ins, and asked to route this to a new ENG ticket.</p><h2 data-local-id=\"f06bcddbea52\">1. Environment and steps to reproduce</h2><p data-local-id=\"10ca0303da30\">Production, tenant 209 tbi, <code>sqldb-prd-wus2-arp-production-209-tbi-platform</code>. Logs from Grafana Explore, <code>grafanacloud-apprissretail-logs</code>, clientId 209. Every query was read only.</p><h3 data-local-id=\"ffe050157a08\">Rachel Dill, 2026-10-13</h3><ol data-local-id=\"bb49940ea271\"><li data-local-id=\"902e5d5117f1\"><p data-local-id=\"6c1fd9cb8de5\">Her row exists in <code>sso.SecurityLevelAssignments</code>: SecurityID 5, Persistent NULL, loaded 2026-10-13 10:42 UTC. <code>EXEC sso.GetUserSecurityLevel</code> returns 5 for her.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"99ad687f4738\"><p data-local-id=\"596b0955ac48\">Her first SSO sign in, 2026-10-13 19:23:49 UTC, creates the account.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"7652fa55984b\"><p data-local-id=\"79e7be8223a8\">Check <code>membership.Users.SecurityID</code>, or Portal, Settings, Users, Rachel Dill, Secure Incident tab.</p></li></ol><p data-local-id=\"24583fd327ce\">Expected: Location Manager, SecurityID 5. Actual: NULL. I set it manually on 2026-10-14. It held after her next sign in on 2026-10-14 19:58 UTC.</p><p data-local-id=\"c85c61956ac7\">Grafana sequence for that sign in:</p><table data-local-id=\"dc3e1ac5-55d0-477b-97b4-275a7940ebbe\"><thead><tr><th data-local-id=\"6a64cba19dda\"><p data-local-id=\"42172a90caac\">UTC</p></th><th data-local-id=\"44c35245d87b\"><p data-local-id=\"6559b7fa3a79\">Sender</p></th><th data-local-id=\"4a6c7d416538\"><p data-local-id=\"facf66eb1d5e\">Message</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-local-id=\"ac89222428ee\"><p data-local-id=\"3c7e7a3d5272\">19:23:49.582</p></td><td data-local-id=\"af2c40ad79d4\"><p data-local-id=\"022f275caa71\">SsoService</p></td><td data-local-id=\"cd92e6bb8f19\"><p data-local-id=\"7c7c07a7585e\">Identified 1 SSO Extra permission groups to assign</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"1dd958b83496\"><p data-local-id=\"aa1369f05a26\">19:23:49.586</p></td><td data-local-id=\"c662b932450d\"><p data-local-id=\"27627ee15d1e\">SsoService</p></td><td data-local-id=\"ac97a0e421e3\"><p data-local-id=\"bf240d8f7a7c\">Identified 1 SSO Extra teams to assign</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"b47a56fad881\"><p data-local-id=\"da1dda065bb2\">19:23:49.641</p></td><td data-local-id=\"5ec7f02c4f84\"><p data-local-id=\"fe2b4b9f8de3\">MembershipService</p></td><td data-local-id=\"7a552879f854\"><p data-local-id=\"880df135a2a2\">User Rachel Dill has been created</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"261f4e37bd48\"><p data-local-id=\"5cb4e713174d\">19:23:49.660</p></td><td data-local-id=\"94b91f758527\"><p data-local-id=\"7ff41ec4dc2d\">SsoService</p></td><td data-local-id=\"afbc321e1844\"><p data-local-id=\"1747a2c335e7\">Sso user created, User Data with <code>&quot;SecurityID&quot;:null</code></p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"6ad82e93d284\"><p data-local-id=\"7a1df93f4b5b\">19:23:49.684</p></td><td data-local-id=\"7f12bda6995c\"><p data-local-id=\"74f5215d18f3\">MembershipService</p></td><td data-local-id=\"e2d13412be6f\"><p data-local-id=\"3bb8bcac3f4e\">Added to ApprissCase Users, Basic Users</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"94b668049ba3\"><p data-local-id=\"51bfdf12d550\">19:23:49.698</p></td><td data-local-id=\"e69e9aad31d0\"><p data-local-id=\"80a02743f28c\">MembershipService</p></td><td data-local-id=\"52572c5553d2\"><p data-local-id=\"1c9f2b47bd81\">Added to Location Manager user team</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"ae7ce29a61e6\"><p data-local-id=\"a58fd551d5e0\">19:23:56.732</p></td><td data-local-id=\"17a1b6bf78d0\"><p data-local-id=\"efeadf019b8c\">Saml2</p></td><td data-local-id=\"daf8d6746f04\"><p data-local-id=\"172646304a49\">Logged on</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p data-local-id=\"c636260830fd\">No line about the security level.</p><h2 data-local-id=\"e2e9c7c1cd81\">2. Findings</h2><p data-local-id=\"0e329de7d368\">Users created through SSO between 2026-10-09 and 2026-10-15, all with level 5 in <code>sso.SecurityLevelAssignments</code>:</p><table data-local-id=\"fc1177c4-54f6-443e-95a0-0785ae109e4b\"><thead><tr><th data-local-id=\"7d0d6857d721\"><p data-local-id=\"f31fda2cba70\">User</p></th><th data-local-id=\"0b9d19a1bd0b\"><p data-local-id=\"14e1567ad82b\">Created UTC</p></th><th data-local-id=\"a70d3ecdfe1b\"><p data-local-id=\"8ab3904adefa\">Last sign in UTC</p></th><th data-local-id=\"aeedbdbcd8f7\"><p data-local-id=\"a0fac7507cc5\">Account level</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-local-id=\"59e3eb440106\"><p data-local-id=\"d2e52e982e75\">Ashley N Carter</p></td><td data-local-id=\"b07cb56599b3\"><p data-local-id=\"1987c4a9bfe6\">10-09 20:24:16</p></td><td data-local-id=\"6d3eca70de18\"><p data-local-id=\"7e92018bbb8f\">10-09 20:27:23</p></td><td data-local-id=\"9acad4fbe505\"><p data-local-id=\"5ad78cf68fc5\">5</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"f686a4eb05f5\"><p data-local-id=\"df7f1098eecc\">Teegan Baker</p></td><td data-local-id=\"b4d85adc7ae2\"><p data-local-id=\"811b303fd9e5\">10-10 17:58:30</p></td><td data-local-id=\"60eb8f32958b\"><p data-local-id=\"5848cab490ca\">10-10 18:00:39</p></td><td data-local-id=\"af6250666ecc\"><p data-local-id=\"2a0c0ce5450b\">5</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"43ac0767c4dd\"><p data-local-id=\"be2e4bd4ca12\">Jordan Shields</p></td><td data-local-id=\"89a30d5da3de\"><p data-local-id=\"8aae15e1fc9d\">10-11 20:44:20</p></td><td data-local-id=\"7929a3a68c1d\"><p data-local-id=\"625ba2326f67\">10-11 20:50:28</p></td><td data-local-id=\"003da22cedcb\"><p data-local-id=\"58a5e4e0ede9\">5</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"6727478d79ca\"><p data-local-id=\"b0c8b664eb30\">Alexis Post</p></td><td data-local-id=\"5a7b3b62693d\"><p data-local-id=\"6e02ad54d63d\">10-13 19:22:23</p></td><td data-local-id=\"c6188297b7ab\"><p data-local-id=\"d60221dc3bc5\">10-13 19:50:47</p></td><td data-local-id=\"4911dab1df85\"><p data-local-id=\"fca262cf074d\">5</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"4754ab16d9a9\"><p data-local-id=\"342fb44711c5\">Theresa Veasley</p></td><td data-local-id=\"d7ab33d643fd\"><p data-local-id=\"5934e051609a\">10-15 17:17:42</p></td><td data-local-id=\"fd32bd96fc55\"><p data-local-id=\"2a7f21dc72d6\">10-15 17:46:18</p></td><td data-local-id=\"05eb26b619bf\"><p data-local-id=\"8c706f85b07d\">5</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"ec02b6cb6050\"><p data-local-id=\"f82b9d1093ba\">Brett Virtue</p></td><td data-local-id=\"2aa4a61a3a83\"><p data-local-id=\"343f1b97c2af\">10-14 19:47:05</p></td><td data-local-id=\"ca383a489124\"><p data-local-id=\"7b085f98343a\">same</p></td><td data-local-id=\"7a44dc480402\"><p data-local-id=\"702514520578\">NULL</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"69c17c804e2f\"><p data-local-id=\"ff864bebd21c\">Doris Mays</p></td><td data-local-id=\"91d25cbee112\"><p data-local-id=\"a0dc3a1b2b52\">10-14 20:00:25</p></td><td data-local-id=\"22b174df5c7c\"><p data-local-id=\"e0089820d4ea\">same</p></td><td data-local-id=\"024d92c019a8\"><p data-local-id=\"ce3d25b5b48a\">NULL</p></td></tr><tr><td data-local-id=\"7f1c0eb23981\"><p data-local-id=\"32618308df4c\">Tamieko Jones</p></td><td data-local-id=\"6c82b7065e85\"><p data-local-id=\"4369713062c0\">10-15 14:00:02</p></td><td data-local-id=\"3dabec1c4750\"><p data-local-id=\"5517dfb7f2e4\">same</p></td><td data-local-id=\"f04330eb1714\"><p data-local-id=\"7fde866516a7\">NULL</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p data-local-id=\"440f6be66927\">Every user who signed in again has the level. Every user whose only sign in created the account does not. Verified.</p><p data-local-id=\"82f17f1fef88\">49 users who signed in since 2026-07-02 have a feed level above 0 and a NULL SecurityID in <code>membership.Users</code> and in the lpuser view. Verified. How many of them signed in only once is not checked yet.</p><p data-local-id=\"199be8d50ea9\"><strong>My reading, unverified:</strong> the security level step is skipped on user creation and runs on later sign ins.</p><h2 data-local-id=\"ba17f98414d7\">3. Troubleshooting performed</h2><p data-local-id=\"620ef9d03c17\">Ruled out so far: the feed, the rows are present; <code>sso.GetUserSecurityLevel</code>, its current definition orders by Persistent with no Persistent = 1 filter and returns 5; the lpuser view, every affected user is in it. Detail in my internal note of 2026-10-14 on <a href=\"https://trebuco.atlassian.net/browse/RCS-28256\" data-card-appearance=\"inline\">https://trebuco.atlassian.net/browse/RCS-28256</a> .</p><p data-local-id=\"d62e28edac75\">Outside the ticket: Teams with Matthew Kamminga on 2026-10-15, and an email thread with J.R. Teagle on the same reports. Workaround in use: setting Incident Security ID manually in the Portal.</p><h2 data-local-id=\"42e0b53c1ef8\">4. Still open</h2><ol data-local-id=\"fc64d4f203bf\"><li data-local-id=\"b6f4b1130181\"><p data-local-id=\"9881da86642f\">Does the SSO user creation path call the security level assignment, and is that the step that is skipped?</p></li><li data-local-id=\"90317a9d756e\"><p data-local-id=\"f7b8dce47999\">Once confirmed, could the affected accounts be corrected in one pass, or should Support set them one by one?</p></li></ol><p data-local-id=\"ad378b039b2e\">Related: <a href=\"https://trebuco.atlassian.net/browse/RCS-28256\" data-card-appearance=\"inline\">https://trebuco.atlassian.net/browse/RCS-28256</a>  and <a href=\"https://trebuco.atlassian.net/browse/RCS-27578\" data-card-appearance=\"inline\">https://trebuco.atlassian.net/browse/RCS-27578</a> .</p>",
